      "side": 0,
      "message": "Well it\u0027s time then to regain some intellectual control!\n\nI assume that if you don\u0027t understand it and I don\u0027t understand it after staring about it a while, then no one understands it and it\u0027s not a good situation to be in.\n\nHow about turning the one \"sanitizeDep\" bit into a set of bits, one for each sanitizer? That way, we don\u0027t need to rely on the interleaving of sanitizerDepsMutator and sanitizerMutator instances and the information flow is top-\u003edown then bottom-\u003eup, thereby making things simpler? (at the cost of a bit of RAM, but TBH I\u0027m more worried about the fact that no one understands the code than about RAM use...)\n\nHow about this plan:\n\n1. I submit this change without the removal `c.SetSanitizeDep(false)`\n2. I submit another change that turns `sanitizeDep` into a set of bits, one for each sanitizer",
